ished":"2026-11-14T23:16:30.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50474063/week-11-live-highlights","type":"Story","byline":"ESPN staff","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Darian Mensah dices up ex-team Duke as Miami rebounds from first loss","description":"Miami quarterback Darian Mensah diced up his former team on Saturday, finishing with 382 yards and a touchdown in the 36-25 victory over Duke.","published":"2026-11-14T23:46:29.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50484151/darian-mensah-dices-ex-team-duke-miami-rebounds-first-loss","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Andrea Adelson","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Wake Forest strengthens CFP case with 'statement' win at SMU","description":"No. 13 Wake Forest made a statement to the College Football Playoff selection committee with a 49-7 blowout of SMU on Saturday.","published":"2026-11-14T22:49:36.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50483729/wake-forest-strengthens-cfp-case-statement-win-smu","type":"HeadlineNews","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Vols lose top receiver Matthews to knee injury vs. Texas A&M","description":"Tennessee leading receiver Mike Matthews suffered a right knee injury in the second quarter of Saturday's game at Texas A&M.","published":"2026-11-14T23:16:10.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50483677/vols-lose-top-receiver-matthews-knee-injury-vs-texas-am","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Mark Schlabach","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Georgia commit, DL Marcellus Young Casario died after 'sudden medical emergency'","description":"Marcellus Young Casario, a Georgia football commit, died Friday after experiencing a \"sudden medical emergency,\" according to his high school.","published":"2026-11-14T20:36:58.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50482223/georgia-football-commit-marcellus-young-casario-dies-suddenly","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Eli Lederman","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Oklahoma AD rips Ole Miss, SEC; Rebels defend travel effort","description":"Oklahoma AD Roger Denny ripped the SEC and Ole Miss for the \"inexplicable\" decision to move its game to Sunday, while the Rebels defended their travel efforts.","published":"2026-11-14T23:10:56.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50482206/oklahoma-ad-infuriated-sec-ole-miss-sunday-game","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Max Olson","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Clemson QB Reynolds to have MRI on knee; backup Vizzina (ankle) also hurt","description":"Clemson quarterback Tait Reynolds is having an MRI on his injured knee while backup Christopher Vizzina was sent to the hospital to evaluate his ankle.","published":"2026-11-14T22:29:42.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50482105/clemson-qb-tait-reynolds-suffers-leg-injury-slide","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Andrea Adelson","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Central Oklahoma AD trolls Ole Miss amid FAA crisis-forced kickoff change","description":"The Division II school offered Ole Miss fans attending its Oklahoma matchup free admission due to the kickoff date change.","published":"2026-11-14T22:28:10.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50481529/central-oklahoma-troll-ole-miss-faa-decsion","type":"Story","byline":"Kalan Hooks","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Ohio State WR Smith sets Big Ten record, states Heisman case","description":"Ohio State wide receiver Jeremiah Smith broke yet another record, eclipsing the Big Ten mark for career receiving yards while also making his Heisman Trophy case in Saturday's win over Northwestern.","published":"2026-11-14T23:15:02.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50481134/ohio-state-jeremiah-smith-sets-big-ten-receiving-record","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Jake Trotter","source":"ESPN"}],"links":{"espn":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/player/_/id/5079518/jaylen-mcclain","wikipedia":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jaylen_McClain"},"wiki":{"rules":4,"title":"Jaylen McClain","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jaylen_McClain","description":"American football player (born 2006)","touched":"2026-11-14T07:37:23Z","intro":"Jaylen McClain (born June 24, 2006) is an American football safety for the Ohio State Buckeyes.","sections":[{"key":"early","title":"Early life","text":"McClain attended high school at Seton Hall Preparatory School located in Essex County, New Jersey. During his junior season, he notched 83 tackles along with two interception, while also scoring an offensive touchdown. Coming out of high school, McClain was rated as a four-star recruit, the 22nd overall safety, and the 243 overall player in the class of 2024, where he committed to play college football for the Ohio State Buckeyes over offers from other schools such as Georgia, Michigan, Michigan State, Notre Dame, Oregon, Rutgers, Penn State, Stanford, Tennessee, and USC."},{"key":"college","title":"College career","text":"During his true freshman season in 2024, he played in all 15 games, notching 15 tackles. Heading into the 2025 season, McClain competed with Malik Hartford for a starting spot in the Buckeyes secondary. Ultimately, he would beat out Hartford, and become the team's starting safety besides Caleb Downs. In week one of the 2025 season, McClain notched eight tackles in a victory over the #1 ranked Texas Longhorns. In week three, he notched a pass deflection, in a 37-9 victory over Ohio."}]}}